// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ending E2 "Dace" (C, 3 min). GOODBYE: DACE. act3_ending.md §2 E2, §0 rule 8; ADR 0022 (i).
// With Imra gone his hands are free for the first time in eleven years; HE TURNS AROUND, and we see his face for the first
// time. He knows Rhen at once. DACE AND KERRID: ONE LOOK, NO WORDS: past Rhen's shoulder he sees Kerrid at the rail; for
// one beat the reach he missed on the Corrow stair is in his face; Kerrid shakes his head once. Then Dace looks only at
// his son. Dace says goodbye, and THIS TIME RHEN SAYS IT BACK, aloud, plainly, never cut away from. Dace sees his old
// lantern on Rhen's shoulder (the first of his pair, left on its hook at Oruvel; still its own oil burner, NOT Kell's
// wick) and is glad. The lantern is UNLIT: Rhen put it out on the dark deck. FRAMING: one slow push-in on the pair (E03);
// the look is a shot (Dace, Kerrid off-frame past Rhen's shoulder: E04) and a reverse single of Kerrid alone at the rail
// (E05), never a three-shot or a two-shot of the two dead; ONE reverse at "Goodbye, Dad." (E06: W23's lens and distance
// on Rhen exactly, the rhyme with Ch8 B17). The current-song stays until after the line. `goodbye_dace`.
title: ending_dace
location: ch18/kite
---
@letterbox on
@light LanternLight off
@camera E03
@music goodbye_dace fade=2.0
@anim dace turn_to rhen
@vfx glimmer_lift at=dace count=20 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 4.0
Dace [tender]: Rhen. #line:ending_dace_001 #tn:"Dace Sallow's first spoken word in the game. Plain, a diver's voice."
@wait 2.0
@camera E04
@anim dace look_at kerrid
@wait 2.5
@camera E05
@anim kerrid shake_head
@wait 2.0
@camera E03
@anim dace look_at rhen
@wait 2.0
Dace [soft_smile]: You took the old one down. Off the hook. #line:ending_dace_002
Rhen [neutral]: The winter I turned nine. #line:ending_dace_003
@wait 2.0
Dace [tender]: Good. It was always the better of the two. #line:ending_dace_004
@wait 3.0
Dace [grief]: I'm sorry, son. I should have come home. #line:ending_dace_005
@wait 3.0
Dace [tender]: Goodbye, Rhen. #line:ending_dace_006
@wait 2.0
@camera E06
Rhen [grief]: Goodbye, Dad. #line:ending_dace_007 #tn:"The payoff of Rhen's arc: this time he says it back. Plain, aloud, no softening."
@wait 3.0
@camera E03
@vfx glimmer_lift at=dace count=60 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 6.0
@letterbox off
===
